      {
        "n": "IN FOCUS: ROY MONTGOMERY (R)",
        "s": "2026-11-14T08:00:00Z",
        "e": "2026-11-14T10:00:00Z",
        "d": "New Zealand guitarist Roy Montgomery's music was once described by NPR journalist Lars Gotrich as \"swimming through phantoms\" – it may sound like an overwrought analogy at first, but simply spend half an hour enveloped in Montgomery's tones, and you'll understand. \nOriginally a part of Pin Group in the 1980s, releasing Joy Division-indebted post-punk on the revered Wellington label Flying Nun records, Montgomery eventually unmoored himself from the strictures of verse-chorus-verse songwriting, and other musicians entirely, composing drifting, gauzy guitar instrumentals that channeled his own personal grief and loneliness into a seductively baleful magic. ",
        "j": "ROY MONTGOMERY",
        "u": "https://www.nts.live/api/v2/shows/in-focus/episodes/in-focus-roy-montgomery-7th-june-2024",
        "t": "restream"
